2026-08-24 @ 15:10 - [Feat - bpa-demo-axa-app.sh: create the "BPA Demo AXA" AXA application and sync its BrowserAgent snippet into .config.example]:
  User asked for a new script to create a DX O2 AXA (Application
  Experience Analytics) application called "BPA Demo AXA" via dx-do and
  update the config template with the resulting snippet, for use in the
  demo environment. This is the first script in this project to manage
  an AXA resource -- a genuinely different type from every other
  telemetry source here (Services, Universes, Management
  Modules/Metric Groupings/Alerts, SLI groups, Dashboards).
  Named "BPA Demo AXA" (not plain "BPA Demo") to avoid colliding with
  the many other tenant resources already using that exact name --
  confirmed via `axa list-applications` that a separately/manually-
  created "BPA Demo" AXA application already exists (its snippet is
  what's currently live in the real, gitignored .config); left it
  untouched, this script creates and manages its own independent one.
  Added dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-axa-app.sh:
  - create: self-heals by name via `axa list-applications` (axa
    create-application has no dry-run at all and rejects duplicate
    names outright -- confirmed via `dx-do help describe`), creates via
    `axa create-application applicationName="BPA Demo AXA" secure=false`
    if missing, then always (re-)fetches the BrowserAgent snippet via
    `axa get-application-snippet` and patches it into .config.example's
    APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET line -- so create also serves as a "resync
    the template" operation on every re-run, even if the application
    already existed.
  - check: prints the application's definition and current snippet,
    and whether .config.example is in sync.
  - delete: deletes the application (irreversible, no dry-run on the
    API side -- prompts for confirmation unless -y/--yes) and resets
    .config.example's APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET back to the empty
    placeholder, since the snippet would otherwise reference a deleted
    application.
  Two landmines found live: (1) `axa get-application-snippet` silently
  ignores output.format=json and always returns pretty-printed,
  multi-line HTML -- fetch_snippet() strips progress noise and blank
  lines, then collapses the rest to the single-line form this
  project's .config already uses elsewhere. (2) the snippet's many /,
  :, and " characters make sed-delimiter or shell-string-interpolation
  patching fragile -- the same class of bug entrypoint.sh's
  bundle.properties patching hit and solved with an unlikely delimiter;
  solved here instead by writing the snippet to a temp file and passing
  file paths into a single-quoted (non-interpolating) python heredoc,
  never embedding the raw value into inline python source.
  The snippet itself is safe to commit into .config.example (unlike
  every other value there) -- it's a client-side <script> tag meant to
  be embedded in every page and visible via view-source, not a secret.
  Verified live: created the application (key 4ab13890-...), confirmed
  via `git diff .config.example` that only the APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET
  line changed, confirmed `bash -n .config.example` still parses as
  valid shell, and re-ran create to confirm idempotency (`axa
  list-applications` shows exactly one "BPA Demo AXA" entry).
  Documented in dxo2-scripts/README.md (new Scripts row + new AXA
  section) and CLAUDE.md's dxo2-scripts narrative.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-08-24 @ 14:30 - [Confirmed - stale-Helm-bundle redirect root cause verified live by the user, fresh bundle resolves it]:
  Follow-up to the entry below. User confirmed the redirect-to-404 was
  caused by deploying a Helm bundle built before the 2026-08-19
  front-controller revert -- its frozen files/vhost.conf still carried
  the old `RewriteRule ^$ /shop [R=302,L]`, and with the old per-page
  wrapper file that used to serve /shop gone post-revert, the redirect
  landed on a 404.
  Built a fresh bundle via `build-scripts/package-helm-bundle.sh`
  (dist/bpa-demo-helm-bundle-1.0.0b18.tar.gz) and verified before
  handing it over: `grep -c RewriteRule` on the bundled vhost.conf
  returns 0, and the bundled file is byte-identical to
  src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf. User redeployed with this fresh
  bundle via `helm upgrade` (build-scripts/deploy.sh) and confirmed the
  fix runs -- no image rebuild was needed, since vhost.conf is rendered
  into the ConfigMap fresh from the chart on every upgrade, not baked
  into the image.
  Documented as a permanent incident note (not just this one fix) in
  CLAUDE.md's "Front controller" section: any previously-built Helm
  bundle must be regenerated before redeploying after an app-code- or
  vhost-affecting change, since package-helm-bundle.sh freezes a real,
  dereferenced copy of vhost.conf at bundle-build time by design (for
  target-host portability), with no staleness warning if that bundle is
  reused later.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-08-24 @ 13:40 - [Docs - fixed a stale mod_rewrite comment in index.php; investigated a reported live redirect]:
  User reported the Kubernetes/Helm deployment redirects to /shop,
  /admin etc., suspecting leftover code from the reverted "URL path
  approach" workaround for the PHP probe's browser-agent injection gate
  (see CLAUDE.md's "Front controller" section -- that workaround was
  fully reverted 2026-08-19, commits b1bf4a4/e82fcda, tags
  revert-to-php-app/query-param-only-routing).
  Searched the entire current repo for any surviving redirect/RewriteRule
  logic: src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf (no RewriteRule directives at
  all), helm/php-demo/templates/ingress.yaml (plain host + path:/ prefix,
  no rewrite annotations), build-scripts/deploy.sh, src/apache-php/
  entrypoint.sh, the Dockerfile, and every header('Location: ...') call
  in app/src/ (all use the index.php?page=... form, none redirect to a
  bare path). Found none -- the current codebase is clean.
  Found one real but purely cosmetic leftover: app/src/index.php's own
  top-of-file comment still said "Apache mod_rewrite maps clean URLs
  (/shop, /basket, /product, etc.) to this file with ?page=<slug>" --
  describing the old, reverted architecture. The actual routing code
  below it was already correct (query-string only); only the comment
  was stale, apparently missed when the revert updated every link/
  redirect elsewhere in the app. Fixed to describe the current,
  no-rewrite behavior.
  Since no redirect logic exists in the current repo, the user's live
  symptom is most likely a stale deployment (an old Helm bundle built
  before the revert, or a Kubernetes release not yet `helm upgrade`d
  against the current chart) rather than a code bug -- following up
  with the user to confirm which, since that determines the fix (rebuild
  the bundle vs. redeploy vs. something not yet found).

