2026-08-24 @ 11:20 - [Fix - bpa-demo-services-universe.sh rewritten for dx-do's o2-universe -> service-universe API replacement]:
  User reported the dx-do maintainer had shipped an API-level fix for
  the long-standing o2-universe console-crash bug (documented in
  dxo2-scripts/dx-do-o2-universe-issue.md since 2026-07-07) and asked
  for this script to be re-checked.
  Confirmed: `o2-universe` no longer exists as a dx-do command group at
  all -- replaced outright by `service-universe`, a full CRUD surface
  (create/update/delete/get/list/export, all dry-run by default) that
  fixes every documented limitation:
  - create/update both take serviceNames= (comma-separated) and produce
    a correctly SERVICE-scoped filter on both the tas and nass views --
    verified live via a `create ... dry-run=true` preview (the default)
    before ever touching the tenant for real; the shape matches the
    console-wizard-created VIEW618/VIEW621 examples exactly.
  - update is a new command -- a drifted serviceNames filter can now be
    corrected without recreating the Universe.
  - delete is now native (viewId= + label= required to match, a
    typo-proof confirmation like dashboard folder-delete) -- the old
    cross-group `apm-universe delete` workaround is no longer needed.
  - Consistent viewId= naming across every subcommand, replacing the
    old create-uses-name=-but-export-uses-universeViewId= inconsistency.
  Rewrote dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-services-universe.sh end to end: create
  now self-heals both by label (if the state file is lost) and by
  filter correctness (re-applies serviceNames via `update` if a tracked
  Universe's SERVICE filter is ever found to have drifted or gone
  missing), restoring the create-from-scratch fallback that had been
  deliberately disabled since the 2026-07-07 crash finding. check/delete
  both moved to the new service-universe commands.
  VIEW618 (the script's previously-tracked instance) no longer exists in
  the tenant -- not investigated when or why. Adopted the tenant's
  existing VIEW621 (label "BPA Demo service universe", created the same
  day as the original VIEW618 workaround, already correctly
  SERVICE-scoped to "BPA-Demo") as the tracked instance instead of
  creating a duplicate -- confirmed via `service-universe get` before
  adopting it, and confirmed no stray Universe was left behind by the
  verification dry-run.
  Verified live: `create` found and adopted VIEW621 via label self-heal;
  `check` prints its full definition; re-running `create` is idempotent
  (no duplicate, no unnecessary update call since the filter was already
  correct).
  Closed out dxo2-scripts/dx-do-o2-universe-issue.md with a resolution
  update; updated CLAUDE.md's dxo2-scripts narrative, TOBEDONE.md's
  Universes/Topology section, and dxo2-scripts/README.md's Scripts table
  to match.

