2026-08-21 @ 14:05 - [Fix - bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh contradictory create/delete after parent Management Module was deleted and recreated]:
  User reported: create says all 12 alerts already exist, delete says none
  of them exist -- for the same ids. Root cause: at some point the "BPA-
  Demo" Management Module was deleted and recreated (mm-3562 -> mm-45705),
  cascade-deleting all 12 child Metric Groupings/Alerts this script had
  created under the old one. .state/bpa-demo-agent-alerts.env never
  detected this and kept referencing the dead ids under the old MM.
  `create` reported "already created" from stale local state, then
  crashed with exit 255 after healing only 1 of 12 keys: heal_one()'s
  metricgrouping update call had no || fallback (unlike its sibling
  list-metrics call), so a 404 from updating a metric grouping whose
  parent MM no longer exists propagated straight through set -euo
  pipefail and killed the script. `delete` technically succeeded for all
  24 resources (12 alerts + 12 metric groupings, each caught by an
  existing || info "already gone." fallback) but printed a noisy raw
  Axios 404 dump for every one, which reasonably read as failure.
  Fixed in dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh:
  - Added grouping_exists() (metricgrouping detail probe, no output).
  - heal_one() now checks grouping_exists first and falls through to
    create_one() (recreate from scratch) instead of attempting a doomed
    update on a nonexistent resource.
  - cmd_delete()'s two delete loops (alerts, metric groupings) now check
    existence first and print a clean "already gone -- nothing to
    delete" message, skipping the delete call entirely instead of
    attempting it and catching the resulting error noise.
  Verified live: `delete` against the genuinely-broken state completed
  cleanly (24 "already gone" messages, no crash, no noisy dumps) and
  removed the stale state file. `create` from the now-clean state
  recreated all 12 metric groupings + alerts fresh under mm-45705 with no
  crash; spot-checked 3 (infra-availability, php-resp-time, browser-
  page-load) via metricgrouping list-metrics output.format=json and
  confirmed each has real live matches (1, 1, and 13 rows respectively).
  Not investigated: why the parent Management Module was deleted and
  recreated in the first place (manual console action vs. a related bug
  in bpa-demo-management-module.sh) -- out of scope for this fix.

