2026-08-21 @ 13:27 - [Feat - rebuilt BPA-Demo SLI/SLO monitoring from scratch under dx-do v7.2.1's SLI-group model]:
  User asked to rebuild SLI/SLO monitoring under the new model, following
  the entry below's finding that the tenant's old sliId 873/2767/2768/2769
  no longer exist. dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-sli.sh was rewritten from scratch
  (the old export/import-based script and its three now-schema-
  incompatible JSON templates deleted -- templates/bpa-demo-response-
  time-sli.json, bpa-demo-error-rate-sli.json, bpa-demo-page-load-time-
  sli.json) to create and self-heal 3 independent SLI groups purely via
  CLI flags (sli create-group/add-slo/add-alert/set-group-filter), no
  files needed:
  - BPA-Demo Frontend Response Time (sliGroupId 2955): average of every
    Frontends|Apps|bpa-demo-*|URLs|<page>:Average Response Time (ms) from
    the PHP probe agent, 5-min aggregation. SLO: LE 200ms objective, 98%
    target, rolling 1-day.
  - BPA-Demo Frontend Error Rate (2956): same shape, Errors Per Interval,
    SLO LE 2.
  - BPA-Demo Client-Side Page Load Time (2957): Business Segment|BPA
    Demo|<page>:Average Page Load Time (ms) from the Browser Agent
    (Logstash-APM-Plugin identity). SLO LE 300ms. Currently registers
    sliStatusCode 5 ("no metrics matching") -- expected, browser-agent
    auto-injection is still reverted so there's no live client-side data,
    same as the original SLI 2769's lifelong totalMetrics: 0 before the
    reset.
  Every group also got an alert on its SLO's rolling percentage (caution
  <98%, danger <90%) -- a genuine improvement over the original three
  SLIs, none of which ever had an alert wired to any SLO.
  Two landmines found live while building this, both documented in the
  script's header comment and DX-O2_MANUAL_CONFIGURATION.md: (1) the
  `regex` filter condition is silently broken by a trailing $ anchor --
  a pattern like foo$ matches zero metrics with no error, the identical
  pattern without the trailing $ matches correctly (the match is
  effectively start-anchored/prefix-style already). Every pattern reused
  from elsewhere in this project needed its trailing $ stripped.
  (2) The PHP probe's app-level metric aggregate (Frontends|Apps|bpa-
  demo-docker:Errors Per Interval, no |URLs| segment) exists in the raw
  NASS catalog but is not visible in sli filter-test's service-scoped
  view for BPA-Demo -- only per-URL variants are. Used the per-URL
  pattern for Error Rate instead (same shape as Response Time), which is
  visible and reliable.
  Verified live: sli status shows 2 of 3 groups healthy (sliStatusCode 0)
  and the third's zero-match status is the expected/documented one;
  re-running bpa-demo-sli.sh create against all 3 already-created groups
  reapplied the filters cleanly (set-group-filter is idempotent) and
  added no duplicate SLO/alert.
  Also removed the now-unused DXO2_TENANT_USER_EMAIL variable from
  .config.example and CLAUDE.md's ".config required variables" section
  -- it was only ever needed by the old script's template-rendering step,
  which no longer exists.
  Updated CLAUDE.md's dxo2-scripts section, TOBEDONE.md's SLI/SLO
  section (closing out every previously-open item: the filter-mixing
  bug, the SLO layer never reaching live resources, no alert on any
  SLO), dxo2-scripts/README.md, and DX-O2_MANUAL_CONFIGURATION.md (its
  SLI section, previously the console-only-workaround record, marked
  superseded since the new CLI path needs no console editing at all;
  condensed the still-useful technical findings from that era as
  institutional knowledge). Also caught and fixed a leftover
  inconsistency from the prior commit: TOBEDONE.md's bpa-demo-universe.sh
  entry still said "not yet fixed" despite that bug having been fixed in
  the same commit.

