2026-08-21 @ 12:39 - [Fix + Finding - bpa-demo-universe.sh's own stale-identity bug fixed; the tenant's SLI subsystem has been reset]:
  User asked to handle the two items flagged at the end of the entry
  below: (1) bpa-demo-universe.sh's separate, older stale-identity bug,
  and (2) whether the newly-updated dx-do v7.2.1 CLI's new sli
  set-sli-filter/set-group-filter commands could finally push the
  long-stuck SLI fixes to the live resources.
  (1) bpa-demo-universe.sh: confirmed via apm-universe export that its
  first two METRIC_SOURCES (pre-DEPLOYMENT_NAME/DEPLOYMENT_POSTFIX
  literals bpa-demo-host/bpa-demo-php-probe/bpa-demo-infra-agent) had
  never actually been added to the live Universe -- this script was
  simply missed in the 2026-07-10 batch fix every other dxo2-scripts/
  file got. The live Universe's names array had separately accumulated
  some deployment-correct-ish entries via manual console edits outside
  this script at some point, but even those still carried the dead
  (/usr/sbin/apache2) suffix and, for Kubernetes, UnknownAgent. Fixed by
  switching the first two sources from per-deployment EXACT literals to
  wildcarded REGEX patterns (reusing the patterns already fixed in
  bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh/bpa-demo-service.sh) and re-ran create.
  Found and fixed a second bug live while verifying: the self-heal's
  presence check used grep -qF against the raw export JSON text, which
  works for EXACT names but not REGEX patterns -- JSON string escaping
  doubles every backslash on the wire, so a pattern's literal \| never
  substring-matches the printed \\|, and re-running create kept
  re-adding duplicate REGEX specifiers every time (confirmed live: two
  duplicate pairs added during testing before this was caught). Fixed
  by escaping the pattern's backslashes before the presence check;
  re-verified a subsequent create reports both as already present with
  no further duplication. apm-universe has no "remove metric source"
  command, so both the pre-existing stale EXACT entries and the two
  duplicate REGEX pairs added during testing remain in the live
  Universe -- harmless (the specifier list is OR'd) but not cleaned up;
  only a from-scratch recreation would remove them, which this fix
  deliberately does not do.
  (2) SLI investigation: the new sli command group cannot push the old
  filter/SLO fixes live, for a more fundamental reason than a CLI
  limitation -- the resources no longer exist. sli list-groups (no
  filter, tenant-wide) returns []; sli export sliGroupId=2767 and
  sliGroupId=873 (the tenant's own unrelated pre-existing example) both
  return an identical null/invalid response; nass query-metadata for
  attribute=BPA-Demo.* (the is_sli:true derived-metric naming
  convention dx-do help slis documents) returns zero metrics. The
  underlying BPA-Demo service and its metrics are unaffected -- sli
  filter-test serviceName=BPA-Demo returns dozens of real matches --
  this is specifically an SLI-layer reset, not a service/metric
  problem. Not determined whether this is a genuine SaaS-side platform
  migration (the new "SLI group" model looks like a real redesign, not
  just a CLI reshuffle) or something tenant-specific. Not acted on
  further -- rebuilding SLI/SLO monitoring under the new model would be
  a fresh creation of new tenant-visible resources, which needs the
  user's sign-off, not something to do unilaterally while investigating
  whether the old ones were reachable.
  Updated CLAUDE.md's dxo2-scripts narrative (bpa-demo-service.sh,
  bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh, bpa-demo-universe.sh, and a new dated entry
  after the SLI/SLO section) and rewrote TOBEDONE.md's SLI/SLO section
