    query-param-only routing, including an open question (not
    investigated) about whether the PHP probe's own
    Frontends|Apps|<app>|URLs|<url> response-time/error-rate metrics --
    the basis for dxo2-scripts/'s alerts and SLIs -- depend on the same
    Frontend-start gate as browser-agent injection, since all of this
    project's nass query verification of those metrics happened while
    the wrapper-file workaround (SCRIPT_NAME never index.php) was active.
  Verified end to end via compose.sh: rebuilt apache-php and traffic
  images; confirmed bare / and index.php?page=shop return 200 while the
  old /shop now correctly 404s; walked a full session by hand (login,
  shop with brand/cap/pagination filters, product view, add-to-basket,
