2026-07-15 @ 09:20 - [Fix - corrected UnknownAgent root cause and wait condition in entrypoint.sh]:
  User reported UnknownAgent still occurring after the 2026-07-10 TCP-port
  wait-loop fix was deployed live, then downloaded a real
  IntroscopeAgent.log directly from a live pod's dx-o2-agent container and
  asked for it to be checked. The log showed the true timeline: the
  PHP-collector port opens and the PHP probe's first ARF connection
  happens ~23-24s after IA startup, but the IA's own WSS connection to the
  Enterprise Manager - the thing the probe's {collector} identity actually
  depends on - does not succeed until ~104s after startup, and only on a
  second attempt (the first failed with a NullPointerException in the
  WebSocket handshake, "Cannot invoke ChannelFuture.await(long) because
  ... handshakeFuture() is null", followed by serverWentAway). The probe's
  identity is resolved (or falls back to UnknownAgent) at that first ARF
  connection, 80+ seconds before the EM session it depends on exists - so
  the previous TCP-port check was checking a condition satisfied long
  before the condition that mattered.
  Replaced the port-check wait loop in src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh with a
  wait on IntroscopeAgent.log itself (already readable from apache-php via
  the shared apmia-share volume) for the literal success line "Connected
  controllable Agent to the Introscope Enterprise Manager", capped at 90s
  (comfortably above the 104s-after-failed-first-attempt case observed),
  same warn-and-continue fallback as before. Verified: bash -n passes;
  grep -Pc '[^\x00-\x7F]' returns 0 (ASCII-only, per the entrypoint coding
  standard); the exact grep condition matches the real downloaded log.
  Updated CLAUDE.md's PHP probe injection section and TOBEDONE.md's
  corresponding entry to reflect the corrected root cause and fix. Not yet
  confirmed live - needs image rebuild + redeploy + a fresh nass query
  check, no cluster access from this sandbox. The downloaded log
  (dump/IntroscopeAgent.log) contains a live JWT and is not committed.

