2026-07-10 @ 12:35 - [Fix - PHP probe race against Infrastructure Agent readiness causes UnknownAgent (hypothesis-driven, pending live confirmation)]:
  User asked to check Broadcom's PHP agent naming docs against the
  UnknownAgent symptom in Kubernetes' PHP probe metric path
  (SuperDomain|bpa-demo-k8s|php-probes|UnknownAgent(/usr/sbin/apache2)).
  Fetched https://techdocs.broadcom.com/.../php-agent-naming-ca-digital-
  experience-insights.html: the metric path's agent-name segment is the
  {collector} variable, "Name of Infrastructure Agent," resolved from
  introscope.agent.agentName at the moment the PHP probe first registers
  with the Infrastructure Agent's PHP-collector socket.
  Root cause: src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh starts Apache immediately with
  no wait for the dx-o2-agent sidecar's collector socket to be listening.
  In Kubernetes, apache-php and dx-o2-agent are separate containers in
  the same pod with no guaranteed start order, and the sidecar's JVM
  cold-start + WSS handshake to the SaaS EM (under a 500m CPU limit) can
  outlast Apache's own startup -- so the PHP probe's first registration
  attempt can race ahead of the Infrastructure Agent resolving its own
  identity and permanently fall back to the generic UnknownAgent
  placeholder for the life of that Apache process. Docker Compose's
  lighter, unconstrained startup profile made it unlikely to lose this
  race, explaining why only Docker resolved correctly (bpa-demo-docker)
  without any fix, confirmed via nass query.
  Fixed by adding a wait loop to src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh before
  Apache starts: polls APMIA_PHP_COLLECTOR_HOST:APMIA_PHP_COLLECTOR_PORT
  via a bash /dev/tcp connect-check every second, up to 60s, warns and
  starts anyway on timeout. Skipped entirely when the probe volume isn't
  mounted (DX O2 not deployed), so a vanilla deployment's startup time is
  unaffected.
  Verified: the exact wait-loop logic in isolation (immediate return on
  success at 0s; warning + continue at exactly the 60s/5s test deadline
  on failure), and inside the real apache-php image (confirmed it
  correctly blocks Apache from starting while the collector port is
  unreachable, and is a complete no-op when the probe volume is absent).
  NOT yet verified against the live effect: this requires rebuilding the
  apache-php image, pushing, redeploying to the Kubernetes cluster (no
  cluster access from this sandbox), and observing whether new PHP-probe
  metrics resolve to bpa-demo-k8s going forward instead of UnknownAgent.
  Files changed: src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh, CLAUDE.md.

