  via nass query that it never appears in the actual reported metric source
  path, so renaming it wouldn't affect console distinguishability; DB
  Monitor's connection hostname property (127.0.0.1 in Kubernetes vs mariadb
  in Compose) and the app's MARIADB_HOST -- both are real connectivity
  requirements dictated by container topology, not identity labels.
  Verified: sourced load_config()/generate_values() from both scripts with
  a test harness -- compose.sh's default (no DEPLOYMENT_POSTFIX set) computes
  all six vars to "bpa-demo-docker"; deploy.sh's default computes all six to
  "bpa-demo-k8s"; `helm lint`/`helm template` confirm the chart's own
