2026-07-09 @ 20:55 - [Fix - root-redirect Location header had the wrong scheme and an exposed internal port]:
  User reported the app unreachable behind Traefik/k8s: hitting
  https://bpa-demo.shdw.fr/ returned a 302 to
  http://bpa-demo.shdw.fr:8080/shop -- wrong scheme (http instead of
  https) and a port (8080) never exposed externally by the
  Ingress/Service. Root cause: src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf's bare-root
  redirect (added earlier for the PHP-probe browser-agent fix -- see the
  Frontend start/SCRIPT_NAME entry above) used a relative substitution,
  `RewriteRule ^$ /shop [R=302,L]`. For an [R] (external) redirect with a
  relative substitution, Apache itself builds the absolute Location header
  via ap_construct_url() -- and Apache has no idea Traefik is terminating
  TLS in front of it, since it only ever serves plain HTTP on :8080. It
  defaulted to scheme http and appended its own listen port. Never caught
  locally because Compose/kubectl port-forward testing has no
  TLS-terminating proxy in front of Apache, so the (coincidentally
  correct-looking) http://host:8080/shop redirect always matched the
  request's real host:port there.
  Fixed by building the redirect as a fully-qualified URL from
  %{HTTP_HOST} (the client-facing Host header, already portless for a
  default port) and a scheme detected from X-Forwarded-Proto (Traefik's
  default header for TLS-terminated requests) or a directly-terminated
  HTTPS connection -- two RewriteRules (an https-branch guarded by
  RewriteCond, falling through to an http-branch) instead of one relative
  substitution.
  File changed: src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf (picked up automatically
  by the Helm ConfigMap via its existing files/vhost.conf symlink -- no
  separate chart edit needed), CLAUDE.md.
  Verified against the real apache-php image (docker run with the edited
  vhost.conf bind-mounted over the baked-in copy): `apache2ctl configtest`
  passes; curl with X-Forwarded-Proto: https set produces
  `Location: https://<host>/shop`; the same request without it (matching
  Compose's no-proxy setup) still produces the original
  `http://<host>:<port>/shop` behavior unchanged.

