2026-07-09 @ 19:05 - [Fix - Helm ConfigMap's vhost.conf had drifted years out of sync]:
  User testing the Helm chart deployment reported the browser-agent
  per-page-wrapper fix "wasn't reflected in the Ingress configuration (or
  Traefik)". Investigated the actual routing mechanism first: the fix is
  entirely internal to Apache's own vhost.conf (mod_rewrite mapping clean
  URLs to per-page wrapper files); the Ingress here is a plain host +
  `path: /` prefix rule with zero rewrite annotations, so it passes every
  request path through to Apache completely unchanged regardless of
  which controller (Traefik, nginx, etc.) is in front of it -- ruled out
  the Ingress/Traefik layer as the cause before looking anywhere else.
  Diffed helm/php-demo/templates/configmap.yaml's embedded vhost.conf
  against the real src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf and found the
  ConfigMap was carrying its own hand-copied literal block that had
  silently drifted: missing the no-cache Cache-Control/Pragma/Expires
  headers entirely, missing the ETag/Last-Modified stripping, missing
  the /health request log suppression, and -- the actual reported
  symptom -- missing the RewriteEngine/RewriteRule pair the per-page
  wrapper files (shop.php, basket.php, etc.) depend on. Kubernetes
  deployments had been running without all of this since whenever the
  ConfigMap was first written; Docker Compose was never affected, since
  it mounts src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf directly with no duplicate
  copy able to drift.
  Fixed the duplication at the root instead of just re-syncing the copy
  (which would only drift again): added helm/php-demo/files/vhost.conf
  as a symlink to src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf, and changed
  configmap.yaml to read it via `{{ .Files.Get "files/vhost.conf" }}`
  instead of embedding a literal copy. Editing the real vhost.conf now
  automatically flows into the next `helm upgrade` -- nothing left to
  remember to keep in sync.
  Verified live: `helm lint`/`helm template` both print an explicit
  "found symbolic link in path... Contents of linked file included and
  used" info line and the rendered ConfigMap now contains the full,
  current vhost.conf byte-for-byte (RewriteRule, cache headers, health
  check suppression, all present). Confirmed the symlink is safe for
  this project's actual deployment path: build-scripts/deploy.sh runs
  `helm upgrade --install php-demo "${chart_dir}"` directly against the
  local chart directory, never `helm package` into a `.tgz` that could
  separate the symlink from its target.
  New: helm/php-demo/files/vhost.conf (symlink, git-tracked as such).
  Changed: helm/php-demo/templates/configmap.yaml.
  CLAUDE.md, README.md: documented the fix and the new single-source-of-
  truth mechanism.

