2026-07-07 @ 17:10 - [Feat - dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-sli.sh: first SLI for BPA-Demo]:
  Added the tenant's first SLI (Service Level Indicator) for BPA-Demo:
  "BPA-Demo Frontend Response Time" (sliId 2767), bound to the "BPA-Demo"
  Service. Modeled directly on the tenant's existing SLIs (found via
  `dx-do sli list` -- 3 pre-existing, all unbound): "Total NonRunning
  Containers" (raw SLI, no SLO) and "CEmperf DB Errors" (full SLO/
  error-budget pipeline). Confirmed via `service metrics serviceName=
  BPA-Demo` that the SLI data model is genuinely different from the
  Alerts already on this project: an SLI's value is computed and written
  onto the Service's own topology vertex (is_sli-tagged), not just a
  threshold on a raw agent metric.
  dx-do's `sli` command group has no native create/delete -- new SLIs are
  made by `sli import`-ing a raw SLI export JSON bound to a target
  service; unbinding uses `sli exclude-service` (no `sli delete` exists).
  Shipped raw-SLI-only for now (average response time across every
  Frontends|Apps|BPA-Demo|URLs|<page> metric from the PHP probe, REGEX-
  scoped to exclude nested Called-Backends/SQL sub-metrics, EXACT-scoped
  to the real probe agent source path) -- deliberately did not attempt
  the SLO/error-budget/alert layer this round: the tenant's two SLO-
  bearing example SLIs use attributeType numeric codes and an
  errorbudget threshold whose exact semantics differ between the two
  examples in ways that couldn't be confirmed from the outside, and
  guessing risked the same silent-zero-match failure mode as the
  agentExpressions bug from 2026-07-06.
  Landmine hit while building the import payload: the raw export's
  groupId (copied from the real existing SLI used as a base) must be
  replaced with a placeholder number (0), not null -- null fails schema
  validation ("expected number, received null"), and leaving the
  original SLI's real numeric id in place risks the importer treating
  the call as an update to that existing SLI rather than a new create.
  Verified end to end against the live tenant, not just created: ran a
  dry-run first (dx-do's default for `sli import`) and confirmed via
  read-only `sli list`/`service slis` that no tenant state changed before
  applying for real with dry-run=false; after applying, confirmed
  enabled=true, totalMetrics=52, sli_compliant=true.
  New: dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-sli.sh (create/check/delete, same convention
  as every other script in this directory), dxo2-scripts/templates/
  bpa-demo-response-time-sli.json (the import payload).
