2026-07-06 @ 19:00 - [Fix - AGENT_EXPRESSION missing SuperDomain prefix; self-heal on both scripts' create]:
  Root cause found while troubleshooting an alert the user reported as
  "linked to no metric tree": bpa-demo-management-module.sh's
  AGENT_EXPRESSION was 'bpa-demo.*' with no 'SuperDomain|' prefix. The
  4-segment MM agentExpressions/metricgrouping sourceNamePattern regime is
  implicitly start-anchored against the FULL 'SuperDomain|<host>|<process>|
  <agent>' path, so a pattern missing that prefix matches zero agents --
  silently: the create succeeds, the alert shows in the console, but
  `metricgrouping list-metrics` (and therefore the alert) has had zero
  matched series since the original setup. Confirmed empirically:
  recreating the identical grouping with an explicit
  sourceNamePattern='SuperDomain\|.*bpa-demo.*' and
  useManagementModuleAgentExpression=false immediately returned 30+ live
  matches; the inherited version returned none.
  dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-management-module.sh: fixed AGENT_EXPRESSION to
  'SuperDomain\|.*bpa-demo.*'; the Metric Grouping create call now passes
  sourceNamePattern + useManagementModuleAgentExpression=false instead of
  inheriting the MM's (broken) agentExpressions. cmd_create now also
  self-heals: if the Management Module already exists, it checks
  `metricgrouping list-metrics` for at least one live match and re-applies
  the fix via `metricgrouping update` if it finds none, instead of treating
  "exists" as "working."
  While troubleshooting this, the user deleted the original Management
  Module (mm-3322) and its Metric Grouping/Alert (mg-3324/simplealert-3325)
  from the tenant. Repaired the live resource in place via
  `metricgrouping update` (0 -> 37 matched series) after re-running create,
  which had landed on a fresh mm-3562/mg-3563/simplealert-3564 since the
  old ids no longer existed. Rebuilt all 12 bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh
  Metric Groupings/Alerts under the new mm-3562 (their own Management
  Module state file now points there); verified all 13 Metric Groupings
  under mm-3562 (the original plus the 12 per-agent/browser ones) have at
  least one live matched series via list-metrics, and all 13 Alerts are
  active.
  dxo2-scripts/README.md, CLAUDE.md: updated the bpa-demo-management-module.sh
  and bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh descriptions to document the bug, the fix,
  and the self-heal behavior; added a general "Landmine" note on the two
  agentExpressions/sourceNamePattern segment regimes (3-segment bare path
  for `metric data`/`agent query-by-regex` vs. 4-segment full path for
  `managementmodule create`/`metricgrouping create/update`) since mixing
  them up is silent and easy to repeat.

