  GRANT SELECT, PROCESS, REPLICATION CLIENT ON *.* every start regardless of
  whether the login already existed, not only on first creation.  Root cause:
  MariaDB's own MARIADB_USER bootstrapping already creates phpuser, scoped
  only to grants on its own database (phpapp.*); the DB Monitor extension
  then failed with "SELECT command denied to user 'phpuser'@'...' for table
  performance_schema.global_variables" because the pre-existing login never
  received the global grant.  CREATE USER IF NOT EXISTS remains a no-op
  (including the password clause) when the login is already present, so an
  existing password is never overwritten -- only the GRANT is reapplied.
  CLAUDE.md: updated the login-verification description to reflect that
  grants are (re-)applied unconditionally, not only for newly created logins.
  Verified: docker exec into mariadb confirms `SHOW GRANTS FOR 'phpuser'@'%'`
  now includes SELECT, PROCESS, BINLOG MONITOR (MariaDB's name for
  REPLICATION CLIENT) ON *.*, and the "SELECT command denied" error no longer
  appears in dxo2 logs after a restart.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-07-02 @ 11:30 - [Fix – DB Monitor "Table performance_schema.global_variables doesn't exist"]:
  Root cause: with grants fixed, the extension's default query set still
  targets MySQL 5.7+ and queries performance_schema.global_variables/
  global_status, which MariaDB does not implement.  The extension bundles an
  alternate query set (config/schema5_6x.json) that queries
  information_schema.global_variables/global_status instead, which MariaDB
  does support -- confirmed via `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM
  information_schema.global_variables` (683 rows) vs the missing
  performance_schema table.
  docker-compose.yml: APMENV_INTROSCOPE_AGENT_DBMONITOR_MYSQL_PROFILES_BPADB_VERSION
  changed from "" to "5_6x", selecting the information_schema-based query set.
  helm/php-demo/values.yaml: added dxo2.dbMonitor.schemaVersion, default "5_6x".
  helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml: the profile VERSION env now reads
  from dxo2.dbMonitor.schemaVersion instead of being hardcoded to "".
  CLAUDE.md: documented the version property and why "5_6x" (not a MySQL
  version match) is the correct setting for MariaDB.
  Verified: dxo2 logs show "Using previous schema version file: .../
  schema5_6x.json" and the "Table ... doesn't exist" error is gone.  One
  cosmetic residual remains: a single calculated metric (total InnoDB memory)
  references the MySQL-only, long-removed innodb_additional_mem_pool_size
  variable and logs a harmless ScriptException every query interval on
  MariaDB; all other DB Monitor metrics collect normally.

