  metrics only expose request/response size in bytes, not extracted field
  values). Measured real response times rather than guessing thresholds:
  normal traffic ~6-7ms, trouble user ~350-690ms on this stack.
  Created via dx-do: Management Module "BPA-Demo" (mm-3322,
  agentExpressions: bpa-demo.* -- matches both the Infrastructure Agent and
  the PHP probe agent), Metric Grouping "BPA-Demo Frontend Response Time"
  (mg-3324, attributeNamePattern matching
  Frontends|Apps|BPA-Demo|URLs|*:Average Response Time (ms) -- every
  tracked frontend URL), and Alert "Trouble User - High Response Time"
  (simplealert-3325, GREATER_THAN, warning=100ms, error=250ms -- both
  comfortably between the measured normal/trouble response time ranges).
  Along the way: discovered managementmodule create executes immediately,
  unlike service/metricgrouping/alert create which default to dry-run --
  accidentally created a throwaway module with a bogus agentExpressions
  value while probing its parameters, caught it, and deleted it
  immediately (confirmed gone via managementmodule list) before creating
  the real one. Also found alert update-simple needs nested
  warningThreshold.threshold=/errorThreshold.threshold= parameters, not
  flat ones (flat ones are silently ignored) -- used to correct the
  alert's thresholds after the initial 1500/3000ms guess turned out to be
  10x too high for the real measured response times.
