  hit /checkout repeatedly) and confirmed via `vertex detail` on both
  checkout business-transaction vertices that the attribute does not yet
  appear, even after restarting the dxo2 container (BTL logs confirm it
  re-fetches its capture-rule cache on startup) and generating fresh
  traffic afterward. Deferred pending further investigation on the tenant
  side; not implemented in this entry.
  New dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-management-module.sh: create|check|delete for
  the above three resources together. Unlike bpa-demo-service.sh, this
  script persists the ids it creates to a local
  dxo2-scripts/.state/bpa-demo-management-module.env file (git-ignored --
  new .gitignore entry for dxo2-scripts/.state/) since dx-do's
  managementmodule/metricgrouping/alert list commands return wrapped table
  output with no raw-JSON mode, making reliable by-name re-lookup
  impractical. create is idempotent (checks the state file's recorded id
  against a fresh managementmodule list before creating); delete removes
  the alert, metric grouping, and management module in dependency order
  and prompts for confirmation unless -y/--yes is passed. Verified end to
  end against the real tenant: check prints live detail for all three
  resources; create correctly no-ops against the already-created ones;
  delete's confirmation prompt aborts without touching tenant state when
  not confirmed (resources confirmed still intact via check afterward).
