2026-06-18 @ 19:00 - [Fix – build number committed only after all images succeed]:
  Previously compute_build_tag() incremented .build_number and wrote the new
  IMAGE_TAG to .config at the start of the build.  If any docker build step
  failed the number was already consumed but no matching image existed.  On the
  next run the number would skip, and the two images (apache-php, dx-o2-agents)
  could end up on different tags if one was skipped in an earlier run.

  compute_build_tag() now only computes FULL_TAG and BUILD_NUM in memory.
  A new commit_build_tag() writes .build_number and updates IMAGE_TAG in .config
  and is called as the very last step before the optional push, after every
  docker build has returned successfully.  Because build.sh uses set -euo
  pipefail, any build failure exits before commit_build_tag() is reached, so
  .config retains the previous tag and no build number is wasted.

  Image refs in the main section now use ${FULL_TAG} directly (rather than
  ${IMAGE_TAG} which was only valid after the old commit-upfront approach).

  File changed: build-scripts/build.sh

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-18 @ 18:00 - [Fix – BTL watchdog in dx-o2-agents entrypoint]:
  The BTListener was started once but never monitored.  If it exited for any
  reason (connection failure, OOM, etc.) it would stay dead for the lifetime
  of the container.

  - _btl_is_alive(): new helper using pgrep -f 'BTListener' to detect the
    Java process regardless of whether BTListener.sh exec's Java directly or
    launches it as a background daemon and exits.
  - _start_btl(): extracted start logic so both initial launch and watchdog
    restarts use the same code path.
  - _btl_watchdog(): new background loop (sleep 30 → pgrep check → restart)
    that keeps the BTL alive as long as the container is running.  Its PID
    is stored in WATCHDOG_PID so the shutdown handler can terminate it cleanly
    before sending SIGTERM to the IA and pkill'ing any remaining BTListener
    Java processes.
  - _shutdown(): updated to kill WATCHDOG_PID first, then AGENT_PID, then
    pkill -f 'BTListener' to catch any BTL process the watchdog may have
    restarted after the PID variable was last updated.

  File changed: src/dx-o2-agents/entrypoint.sh

