2026-06-18 @ 16:00 - [Feat – locked use case; blocks user login]:
  New use case 'locked' that prevents the assigned user from logging in.
  When the login form is submitted with valid credentials but the account
  has the locked use case assigned, auth_login() succeeds internally but
  login.php detects the use case immediately, revokes all session auth
  keys, and displays the error message without ever granting access.
  If a locked use case is assigned to an already-logged-in user, the next
  request triggers usecase_locked() which evicts the session auth data,
  stores a flash message, and redirects to the login page.

  - app/src/usecases/locked.php: new use-case function usecase_locked();
    clears auth session keys, regenerates session ID, stores flash error,
    redirects to ?page=login.
  - app/src/pages/login.php: reads and clears $_SESSION['login_error']
    flash before the already-logged-in redirect; adds elseif branch after
    successful auth_login() to check $_SESSION['usecase'] === 'locked',
    revoke session keys, and set the error inline.
  - helm/php-demo/sql/seed.sql: added demo user id=14 'locked' / 'Laura
    Locked' with the locked use case pre-assigned by the admin.
  - README.md: demo accounts table updated with the locked entry.

