2026-06-17 @ 10:30 - [Fix – Apache startup warnings in apache-php container]:
  Two warnings appeared on every container start:

  1. "AH00558: Could not reliably determine the server's fully qualified
     domain name" – Apache requires a global ServerName directive; a
     VirtualHost-level ServerAdmin is not sufficient.
     Fix: added ServerName localhost to a new conf-available/servername.conf
     and enabled it with a2enconf servername in the Dockerfile.

  2. "/etc/apache2/envvars: line 7: APACHE_CONFDIR: unbound variable" –
     the envvars file references $APACHE_CONFDIR before setting it; with
     set -euo pipefail active this aborts the script under nounset (-u).
     Fix: wrap the `. /etc/apache2/envvars` call with set +u / set -u in
     entrypoint.sh.

  src/apache-php/Dockerfile:
  - Added RUN echo "ServerName localhost" + a2enconf servername.

  src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh:
  - Added set +u before and set -u after `. /etc/apache2/envvars`.

