2026-06-15 @ 18:00 - [Phase 5 – Helm Chart DX O2 Integration & Security Hardening]:
  Extended the php-demo Helm chart (helm/php-demo/) with conditional Broadcom
  DX O2 agent injection via the Kubernetes init-container pattern, and applied
  container-level security context hardening throughout.

  Task 5.1 – DX O2 Agent Sidecar (deployment.yaml):
  - New initContainer dxo2-init: runs the dx-o2-agents image, copies
    /opt/apmia/ → emptyDir volume /apmia-share using `cp -a` (preserves
    permissions and symlinks).  Logs entry count on completion.
    Enabled only when dxo2.enabled=true.
  - New sidecar container dx-o2-agent: runs the actual Infrastructure Agent
    daemon (APMIA Java process + BTL binary) for the lifetime of the pod.
    Receives APMIA_HOME, APMIA_EM_HOST, APMIA_EM_PORT, APMIA_AGENT_NAME,
    APMIA_APP_NAME, APMIA_LOG_LEVEL as environment variables from values.
    dxo2.emHost is validated via Helm `required` so deployment fails fast
    when enabled=true but the EM host is not configured.
    Enabled only when dxo2.enabled=true.
  - nginx container: conditionally sets APMIA_HOME env var and mounts
    apmia-share at /opt/apmia (readOnly: true) when dxo2.enabled=true.
    Entrypoint's BPA plugin injection block reads from this mount.
  - php-fpm container: conditionally sets APMIA_HOME env var and mounts
    apmia-share at /opt/apmia (readOnly: true) when dxo2.enabled=true.
    Entrypoint's PHP probe injection block reads from this mount.
  - New emptyDir volume apmia-share: declared only when dxo2.enabled=true.
  - Pod annotations: adds dxo2.broadcom.com/em-host and /agent-name
    annotations when dxo2.enabled=true for observability tooling discovery.
  - ConfigMap checksum annotation added so pods are automatically recreated
    when nginx or PHP-FPM configuration changes.

  Task 5.2 – Container Security Contexts:
  - allowPrivilegeEscalation: false applied to all containers and init-
    containers: nginx, php-fpm, mariadb, dxo2-init, dx-o2-agent,
    mariadb-lock-cleanup.
  - readOnlyRootFilesystem: false retained for nginx (writes temp files to
    /tmp emptyDir) and php-fpm (probe install writes to /etc/php/8.1/).
  - runAsNonRoot documented with justification comments on all containers:
      nginx:    false – master must bind ports and manage workers
      php-fpm:  false – master starts as root then drops to www-data
      mariadb:  false – official image initialises as root then drops
      dxo2:     false – APMIA installer creates root-owned files in
                        /opt/apmia/logs and /opt/apmia/config

  Task 5.3 – values.yaml (extended):
  - Added image.dxo2 section: repository, tag, pullPolicy (Always).
  - Added top-level dxo2 section:
      enabled:    false (default – no agent, no emptyDir, no sidecar)
      emHost:     "" (empty = disabled; set via .config → values.local.yaml)
      emPort:     "5001"
      agentName:  "bpa-demo-agent"
      appName:    "BPA-Demo"
      logLevel:   "INFO"
      resources:  requests 256Mi/50m, limits 512Mi/500m
  - Inline comments explain the emptyDir sharing pattern and the graceful
    degradation behaviour when enabled=false.

  Task 5.4 – ConfigMap (nginx.conf):
  - Added `include /etc/nginx/modules-enabled/*.conf;` at the top-level
    scope before worker_processes (required by NGINX for dynamic module
    loading).  This matches the directive added to src/nginx/config/nginx.conf
    in Phase 3.  Without it the ConfigMap-supplied nginx.conf would suppress
    the image-level include and BPA module injection would silently fail.

  Task 5.5 – NOTES.txt:
  - Post-install notes show DX O2 status (enabled/disabled) and EM endpoint.
  - Pod layout ASCII updated with DX O2 sidecar and emptyDir annotations
    when dxo2.enabled=true; shows baseline three-container layout otherwise.
  - When disabled, notes include the .config variables to set to activate
    monitoring on the next deploy.

  Task 5.6 – Chart.yaml:
  - Bumped chart version 0.1.0 → 0.2.0.
  - Updated description to mention the DX O2 sidecar.
  - Added broadcom, dx-o2, apmia keywords.

